  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1251 PM MST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nWinds will prevail from the south-southeast this afternoon as the\ncold front has moved well to our east. Temperatures for the\nentire region are set to be 2 to 7 degrees below average as cold,\ndry air filters in underneath an upper-level ridge. Precipitation\nchances are near-zero for the region this afternoon.\n\nSome models, like the GFS, are trending toward a fast-moving \nupper-level disturbance moving through the area Monday night and \ninto Tuesday morning, which could give the Sacramento Mountains a \nchance of snow. The RRFS is deeper and stronger, grazing lower\nOtero County and upper El Paso and Hudspeth Counties with light\nrain early Tuesday morning. With the RRFS' short track record, I\nthink this scenario is a little strong, so I have limited PoPs\nmainly to the Sacramento Mountains for early Tuesday.\n\nCalm weather returns for Wednesday as a new ridge moves through,\nthough another upper-level trough arrives for Thanksgiving. Both\nmodels are trending drier with this trough, though the GFS has a\ncutoff low whereas the ECMWF does not. Another ridge begins to\nform by next weekend.",
